### 2. tp

#### [MODIFY] [dist_utils.py](file:///c:/Users/chris/Downloads/hrm_flashrenderer/tp/dist_utils.py)

[init_dist](file:///c:/Users/chris/Downloads/hrm_flashrenderer/tp/dist_utils.py#16-25) / [init_dist_env](file:///c:/Users/chris/Downloads/hrm_flashrenderer/tp/dist_utils.py#8-15) bekommen ein `backend` Parameter (default `'nccl'`). Wenn `device == 'cpu'`, wird `backend='gloo'` verwendet. `torch.cuda.set_device()` wird nur aufgerufen wenn CUDA vorhanden.

#### [MODIFY] [norm.py](file:///c:/Users/chris/Downloads/hrm_flashrenderer/tp/norm.py)

Hardcoded `device='cuda'` → `device` Parameter (default `'cuda'` für Rückwärtskompatibilität).

#### [MODIFY] [vocab_parallel.py](file:///c:/Users/chris/Downloads/hrm_flashrenderer/tp/vocab_parallel.py)

Identisch: `device='cuda'` → `device` Parameter.

#### [MODIFY] [parallel_linear.py](file:///c:/Users/chris/Downloads/hrm_flashrenderer/tp/parallel_linear.py)

Identisch: `device='cuda'` → `device` Parameter.

